[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Whiskers.Forest_Interaction_phase} == 1:
	join Thorinn leftmost
	join Whiskers rightmost
	if {Whiskers.New_Dialog} == true:
		set {Whiskers.New_Dialog} = false
		Thorinn: Hey there, little one. What are you doing all the way out here, huh?
		Whiskers: *shivering* Me-me-meow
		Thorinn: You’re freezing! Hang tight, I’ll get a fire going for you over at that abandoned fireplace.
	else:
		Whiskers: *shivers*
		Thorinn: I should hurry up and get this campfire going.
elif {Whiskers.Forest_Interaction_phase} == 2:
	join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
	join Whiskers rightmost
	if {Whiskers.New_Dialog} == true:
		Thorinn: There you go, buddy. Bet that feels better, huh?
		Thorinn: You’ve got some serious whiskers on you for such a small fella.
		Thorinn (agitated): Hmm, Whiskers...
		Thorinn (normal): Yeah, I think I’ll call you Whiskers. What do you think?
		Whiskers: I like it! Fits me, don’t you think?
		Thorinn (surprised): Wait, WHAT?! You can TALK?
		Thorinn: Am I losing my mind? Two days in the woods, no food... yeah, this can’t be. I’m definitely hallucinating.
		Whiskers: Relax, Thorinn! You’re not crazy. I can talk, but only to you. Why?  Well...
		Whiskers: Let’s just say, it’s complicated. For now, you’ll just have to trust me. And don’t worry, I’m on your side.
		Whiskers: Let it be known... your choices matter. Big time. Call it karma, fate,
		Whiskers: or cosmic scales... Every decision you make will come back to you. So, just, choose wisely.
		Thorinn (normal): Well, that’s... oddly comforting, I guess? Are you feeling better now?
		Whiskers: Thanks to you, I’m warmed up again. But I could use a little something to eat. Got any fish handy? Maybe cooked over that lovely fire of yours?
		- Sure, I could use something to eat myself.
			Whiskers: There should be a river up ahead. See if you can catch a fish for us there.
			[signal arg="start_fish_quest"]
			set {Whiskers.Accepted_Fish_Quest} = true
			set {Whiskers.New_Dialog} = false
		- No, ignore Whiskers.
			leave Whiskers
			[signal arg="hugo_encounter"]
		- I've already saved you once today, you ungrateful thing.
			Whiskers: Fine I'll go and find my own food.
			leave Whiskers
			set {Whiskers.Shoo_away} = true
			[signal arg="cat_leaves"]
			[signal arg="hugo_encounter"]
	else:
		Whiskers: There should be a river up ahead. See if you can catch a fish for us there.
elif {Whiskers.Forest_Interaction_phase} == 3:
	join Thorinn leftmost
	Hey!
	[signal arg="thorinn_looks_right"]
	Thorinn: !!!
	[wait time="2.0"]
	join Hugo rightmost
	Hugo: Evening, stranger. You don’t look like you’re from around here.
	Hugo: Are you perhaps a traveler?
	Thorinn: Who are you!?
	Hugo: I’m Hugo. I saw your campfire while collecting my ingredients for supper at my inn.
	Thorinn: An inn? I'm actually trying to find my way to a small village called Rockfall. But I've lost my way as soon as it got darker.
	Hugo: You're in luck. I’ve lived in Rockfall my entire life, so I know this forest by heart.
	Hugo: Can I help you get there? The village is not that far anymore.
	- Yes
		Hugo: Then come along traveller, you must be tired from your journey.
		Hugo: I'll show you to my inn.
		set {Hugo.Followed_to_rockfall} = true
		[signal arg="follow_hugo"]
	- No
		Hugo: You will have your reasons. Then I'll be on my way.
		Hugo: You're welcome to stay at my inn once you arrive.
		[signal arg="leave_hugo"]
		leave Hugo
		[wait time="4.0"]
